   "title": "GNI per capita 'almost certain' to reach $40,000 in 2026: finance ministry",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/economy/20261027/gni-per-capita-almost-certain-to-reach-40000-in-2026-finance-ministry",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 02:22:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1793067723.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "Korea is \"almost certain\" to reach a gross national income (GNI) per capita of $40,000 this year, the finance ministry said Tuesday, as Asia's No. 4 economy grew 1 percent in the third quarter from the previous three-month period, driven by strong exports and investment.",
   "summary_zh": "韩国财政部周二表示，韩国今年“几乎确定”实现人均国民总收入（GNI）4万美元。作为亚洲第四大经济体，韩国第三季度较此前三个月增长1%，得益于强劲的出口和投资。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Korea is \"almost certain\" to reach a gross national income (GNI) per capita of $40,000 this year, the finance ministry said Tuesday, as Asia's No. 4 economy grew 1 percent in the third quarter from the previous three-month period, driven by strong exports and investment. The Ministry of Finance and Economy made the assessment following the release of advance third-quarter data from the Bank of Korea (BOK), which would mark a new milestone after the country's per capita GNI, a gauge of the population's purchasing power, first surpassed the $30,000 mark in 2014. \"Korea maintained solid growth despite a high base effect from the first half, raising the possibility of growth in the mid-3 percent range this year,\" the finance ministry said. Finance Minister Lee Hyoung-il said this month Korea's economic growth for 2026 could range from 3.4 percent to 3.6 percent. \"The GNI per capita is almost certain to hit $40,000 for the first time ever,\" it added. The International Monetary Fund also recently projected Korea's per capita GNI would reach the $40,000 level in 2026 and $50,000 in 2028. The finance ministry, however, noted Korea faces structural challenges despite the strong growth, including mounting livelihood-related challenges and disparities across various areas. \"The government intends to tackle the livelihood issues and ease disparities so the benefits of economic growth can be felt in people's daily lives,\" the finance ministry added",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
