   "source": "hindustantimes.com",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 07:29:18 +0530",
   "_dt": 1793066358.0,
   "ageDays": 0.04,
   "summary": "Delhi recorded the season’s lowest minimum temperature for a second straight day on Monday, and its air quality worsened, though it stayed in the “moderate” category. The minimum was 16.2°C, 0.8 degrees lower than Sunday’s 17°C, the previous low for the season. The 24-hour average air quality index ( AQI ) was 174 in the Central Pollution Control Board ’s (CPCB) 4pm bulletin on Monday, up from 153 on Sunday.",
   "summary_zh": "德里周一连续第二天录得当季最低最低气温，空气质量也进一步恶化，不过仍处于“中度”类别。最低气温为16.2°C，比周日的17°C低0.8度，后者是本季此前的最低纪录。中央污染控制委员会（CPCB）周一下午4点的公报显示，24小时平均空气质量指数（AQI）为174，高于周日的153。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Delhi recorded the season’s lowest minimum temperature for a second straight day on Monday, and its air quality worsened, though it stayed in the “moderate” category. The minimum was 16.2°C, 0.8 degrees lower than Sunday’s 17°C, the previous low for the season. The maximum was 31.4°C. The India Meteorological Department (IMD) expects temperatures to fall further, with light rain likely on Thursday and Friday from a cyclonic system over the Bay of Bengal. The 24-hour average air quality index ( AQI ) was 174 in the Central Pollution Control Board ’s (CPCB) 4pm bulletin on Monday, up from 153 on Sunday. Also Read | The pollutants in Delhi's air, and why they are hard to trace As the Capital headed into the new week, the weather held the night’s pollution close to the ground, according to an HT analysis of IMD’s weather-balloon readings from Safdarjung . At 4.30am, a layer of warm air (an inversion) sat about 200 metres above the city, lower than Sunday’s 300 metres, and the air near the ground at Safdarjung was calm overnight. Also Read | Delhi set to witness more rain, cooler days this week, says IMD forecast The evening brought no relief. Safdarjung airfield reported calm air in all five of its reports between 4pm and 9.30pm, and no rain. Readings varied across the city. At 9pm, 13 of the 57 stations reporting an AQI were in the “poor” category, 42 were “moderate” and two were “satisfactory”, according to CPCB data. To be sure, the air quality has been better than in previous years. The AQI averaged 199, the second-lowest for that week in the 12 years since 2015, according to HT’s analysis. The week includes Dussehra, on October 20",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
   "country": [
    "in"
   ],
   "topic": [
    "pol"
   ],
   "tier": 4,
   "actor": "第三方",
