   "title": "2027 polls: INEC opens online access to preliminary voters’ register",
   "url": "https://dailytrust.com/2027-polls-inec-opens-online-access-to-preliminary-voters-register/",
   "domain": "dailytrust.com",
   "source": "Daily Trust（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:03:44 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793063024.0,
   "ageDays": 0.08,
   "summary": "The Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) has made the preliminary register of voters for the 2027 general election available online following concerns over the accessibility of the register. “Accordingly, and in furtherance of its commitment to transparency, accessibility and public confidence in the electoral process, the Commission has decided to make available on its online platform the same Preliminary Register of Voters earlier displayed at the Registration Areas,” the statement said.",
   "summary_zh": "独立国家选举委员会（INEC）在有人担忧选民名册可查阅性之后，已在网上提供2027年大选选民初步名册。声明称：“因此，为进一步践行其对选举进程透明、可获取及提升公众信心的承诺，委员会决定在网上平台提供此前在登记区展示的同一份《选民初步名册》。”",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) has made the preliminary register of voters for the 2027 general election available online following concerns over the accessibility of the register. The commission, in a statement issued on Monday by Mohammed Kudu Haruna, Chairman of its Information and Voter Education Committee (IVEC), said the online publication was an additional measure to complement the physical display of the register conducted nationwide from October 9 to 15, 2026. INEC said the exercise was conducted in accordance with Section 19 of the Electoral Act, 2026, to enable registered voters to inspect their particulars and submit claims and objections as prescribed by law. The commission said it had taken note of concerns raised by Nigerians and other stakeholders over the need to make the register accessible online in addition to the physical display at registration areas. “Accordingly, and in furtherance of its commitment to transparency, accessibility and public confidence in the electoral process, the Commission has decided to make available on its online platform the same Preliminary Register of Voters earlier displayed at the Registration Areas,” the statement said. The register can be accessed through https://display.inecnigeria.org. INEC said the online platform was intended to facilitate wider public access to the register, while processing of claims and objections arising from the exercise continued. It added that the process would precede the certification and publication of the final register of voters scheduled for December 15, 2026. The commission appreciated the continued interest and constructive engagement of Nigerians and other stakeholders, reaffirming its commitment to transparency, accountability and the implementation of the Electoral Act, 2026, towards delivering credible elections. Join Daily Trust WhatsApp Community For Quick Access To News and Happenings Around You",
