   "title": "Putellas wins third Women’s Ballon d’Or",
   "url": "https://punchng.com/putellas-wins-third-womens-ballon-dor/",
   "domain": "punchng.com",
   "source": "Punch（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:52:14 +0000",
   "_dt": 1793058734.0,
   "ageDays": 0.13,
   "summary": "Spanish midfielder Alexia Putellas has won the 2026 Women’s Ballon d’Or, claiming the award for the third time at the ceremony in London on Monday. Putellas ended Aitana Bonmatí’s three-year run as winner of the award. Bonmatí won the Women’s Ballon d’Or in 2023, 2024 and 2025 but was not nominated for this year’s prize.",
   "summary_zh": "西班牙中场球员阿莱xia·普特拉斯于周一在伦敦举行的颁奖典礼上赢得2026年金球奖（Women’s Ballon d’Or），这是她第三次获得该奖项。普特拉斯终结了艾塔娜·博马蒂连续三年获奖的纪录。博马蒂曾于2023年、2024年和2025年获得女足金球奖，但未获本届奖项提名。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Spanish midfielder Alexia Putellas has won the 2026 Women’s Ballon d’Or, claiming the award for the third time at the ceremony in London on Monday. The London City Lionesses star previously won the prestigious individual prize in 2021 and 2022, becoming a three-time winner of the award. Putellas ended Aitana Bonmatí’s three-year run as winner of the award. Bonmatí won the Women’s Ballon d’Or in 2023, 2024 and 2025 but was not nominated for this year’s prize. Putellas captained Barcelona during the 2025/26 season before joining London City Lionesses in the summer. She helped the Spanish club win four trophies, including the Women’s Champions League, Liga F, the Spanish Super Cup and the Copa de la Reina. The 32-year-old also helped Spain win the Women’s Nations League, further strengthening her credentials for the award. Okiki is a journalist with over seven years experience covering politics, foreign news, society, entertainment and the film industry",
   "bodyLevel": "fulltext",
